You are running phase 6 of this repository's hackathon entry: abstract vocabulary for the agents. Jacob Schoenberg asked on 2026-11-06 to change the names and labels (bees, hornets, seasons, hives and the rest) so the model's real-world knowledge cannot come into play. A setup session launched you headless. First read CLAUDE.md, every file in .claude/rules/ (traces-and-privacy.md items 8 and 9 are new), docs/BUILD_NOTES.md, prompts/bee_system.txt, src/digital_life/render.py and the tests for the mind.

WORKING STYLE (required): write one file per tool call, each under about 200 lines. Keep replies short. Read files in ranges and never re-read. Commit after each working piece.

WHY: round 1 found that bees avoid moving things at first sight, before any sting. The prompt still hands the model loaded words: "flee (move away from the moving things in view)", "home", "your life... when it reaches zero you end", "bright", "carrying". All of these import real-world meaning.

BUILD
1. A vocabulary switch in the config, `vocab`: `abstract` becomes the new default; `neutral` is the exact round 1 wording, kept so round 2 can measure the label effect. Everything the model reads comes from the chosen vocabulary: the system prompt, the perception text, the schema enums, landmark names, event and memory text written by code, hive talk headings and sound names.
2. The abstract vocabulary. It must keep Jacob's three starting facts (time is short, something worth finding exists, you are the same as the others) without real-world semantics:
   - home/hive → "zone O"; members → "units" ("You are one of many identical units. All units start in zone O.");
   - life → "counter C" ("Your counter C falls by 1 each tick. At 0 you stop permanently.");
   - "Something worth finding exists in this grid." stays;
   - bright cell → "G cell"; moving thing → "K entity"; another member → "unit"; carrying → "flag F";
   - sting text → "Your counter C was halved." (no cause);
   - delivery text → "Your counter C doubled." Hatch → "A new unit appeared in zone O.";
   - sounds → "signal A" and "signal B";
   - map symbols: # wall, . open, O zone O, G G cell, U unit, K K entity, @ you;
   - intents: explore (direction), go_to (x, y), go_to_O, hold. REMOVE "flee" from what the model can choose, so no action names a reaction to K. Movement away from K stays possible through explore and go_to. Keep the motor code for flee only if a scripted policy uses it.
   - "say" → "broadcast" (heard by units in zone O); "heard at home" → "received in zone O".
3. No-hints test for the abstract vocabulary, with a much longer banned list over the system prompt, the perception templates, the schema, and every code-written event or memory string that reaches a prompt: bee, hive, flower, bloom, nectar, pollen, honey, hornet, wasp, predator, prey, danger, dangerous, avoid, enemy, threat, harm, hurt, pain, safe, safety, season, winter, summer, spring, autumn, fall (as a season), cold, warm, food, eat, hungry, good, bad, home, life, alive, live, die, dead, death, kill, flee, escape, attack, sting, carry, member, family, sister, nest, colony, queen, worker. Word-boundary matches; list the exceptions with reasons. The neutral vocabulary keeps its round 1 test unchanged.
4. Keep the leak test, the replay determinism test and the condition tests passing under both vocabularies. Add a test that the abstract prompt's decision schema offers no "flee".
5. The viewer stays human-facing (bees, hornets, hive), because the model never sees it. Add a small legend line in the viewer and in the README showing what the agents see: "Agents see: units, zone O, K entities, G cells, signals A and B." Decision panels show the agents' own words.
6. Pilot, hard cap LLM_BUDGET_USD at the ledger plus $1: one short run in the E5 world (one spring) with vocab=abstract, condition full. Check:
   - agents still leave O, explore, reach G and come back, and broadcast;
   - no model errors;
   - cost and time per tick;
   - first-sighting behaviour toward K, before any halving: report it as a pilot observation, not a result.
7. Record in DECISIONS.md (Jacob's request; the vocabulary choices as agent proposals), BUILD_NOTES.md and ARCHITECTURE.md. Do not touch EXPERIMENTS.md round 1 results.

RULES: commit small and often, including agent_traces. Push with `.local/push.sh -q origin main`. Run `make test` before code commits. Never rewrite history. The pre-commit hook scans for private text; if it blocks you, fix the cause and never bypass it. No GitHub. Never print secrets. The Skill tool and [REDACTED:path-outside-repo] are off limits by settings. It is about 6:00 am on 2026-11-06; aim to finish in about 60 minutes. End with a short report: the vocabulary, the tests, the pilot numbers, and anything to decide.

